      "problem": "${\\int }_{1}^{e}(\\frac{1}{x}+1)\\,\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "Splitting up the integral into the sum of two integrals and evaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}(\\frac{1}{x}+1)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{e}1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x{|}_{1}^{e}+x{|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡e-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)+(e-1) \\\\  & =1+e-1 \\\\  & =e\\end{aligned}\n$$",
